l conversation. A short self-introduction often uses a name and です. Personal names are not a reason to ask for legal identity details.","objectives":["Say a chosen name","Ask someone's name politely","Express a simple preference"],"grammar":"The object of an action can be marked with を, pronounced o. 本を読みます means I read a book; 水を飲みます means I drink water.","writing":"Optional: explore Kana names and the particles は and が in short sentences.","roles":[["Morning Routine"],["Family"],["School & Work"],["Everyday Actions"],["Unit Review"]],"words":[["本を読みます。","I read a book.","Hon o yomimasu."],["水を飲みます。","I drink water.","Mizu o nomimasu."],["ご飯を食べます。","I eat a meal.","Gohan o tabemasu."],["日本語を勉強します。","I study Japanese.","Nihongo o benkyō shimasu."],["寝ます。","I go to bed / sleep.","Nemasu."]],"scenario":{"prompt":"Aki introduces themself. You want to ask your next guide's name politely. Choose your question.","answer":"お名前は何ですか。","choices":["お名前は何ですか。","ねこが好きです。","私もです。"],"explanation":"お名前は何ですか asks someone's name; the other choices express a preference or agreement."},"source":"tokyo-guide"},"Asking for the Bill":{"slug":"kyoto-tea-house","location":"Kyoto Tea House","aliases":["Food & Eating Out"],"culture":"Tea houses and cafés differ in how they serve guests. This fictional café lets you practice a short order. Ask about ingredients when necessary rather than assuming every dish is suitable for you.","objectives":["Ask for water or tea","Use a polite request","Thank someone after receiving an order"],"grammar":"お会計をお願いします is a polite way to ask for the bill. Payment procedures differ by restaurant. カードは使えますか asks whether card payment is available.","writing":"Optional: compare おちゃ in Hiragana with お茶. Learn 茶 in a word rather than in isolation.","roles":[["Food & Drinks"],["At a Café","At a Cafe"],["Ordering Food"],["Restaurant Conversation"],["Unit Review"]],"words":[["お会計をお願いします。","The bill, please.","Okaikei o onegaishimasu."],["カードは使えますか。","Can I pay by card?","Kādo wa tsukaemasu ka."],["現金","Cash","genkin"],["カード","Card","kādo"],["ごちそうさまでした。","Thank you for the meal.","Gochisōsama deshita."]],"scenario":{"prompt":"You are ready to order one tea. Which complete request fits?","answer":"お茶を一つください。","choices":["お茶を一つください。","水をください。","ありがとうございます。"],"explanation":"お茶を一つください requests one tea. 水をください requests water; thanks alone does not place an order."},"source":"kyoto-tea-house"}},"units":[{"slug":"tokyo-greetings","location":"Welcome to Tokyo","aliases":["Greetings & Introductions"],"culture":"Tokyo is a setting for your first everyday exchanges. Choose greetings for the time of day and the relationship; there is no single greeting for every situation.","objectives":["Greet someone during the day and in the morning","Get attention politely","Close a short exchange with thanks"],"grammar":"ございます makes おはようございます a polite morning greeting. すみません can get someone's attention or express an apology. Keep the long vowel in ありがとう; romanization is a reading aid, not English spelling.","writing":"Optional: try Hiragana vowels and notice how こんにちは is written with は, pronounced wa in this greeting.","roles":[["Saying Hello","Hello and goodbye"],["Introducing Yourself"],["Asking Someone's Name"],["Basic Conversation"],["Unit Review"]],"words":[["こんにちは","Hello (daytime)","konnichiwa"],["おはようございます","Good morning (polite)","ohayō gozaimasu"],["こんばんは","Good evening","konbanwa"],["すみません","Excuse me / sorry","sumimasen"],["ありがとうございます","Thank you (polite)","arigatō gozaimasu"],["またね","See you (casual)","mata ne"]],"scenario":{"prompt":"You meet your guide at nine in the morning. Which polite greeting fits?","answer":"おはようございます","choices":["おはようございます","こんばんは","またね"],"explanation":"おはようございます is a polite morning greeting. こんばんは is used in the evening; またね is a casual farewell."}},{"slug":"tokyo-numbers","location":"Tokyo Convenience Store","aliases":["Numbers & Time"],"culture":"A convenience store gives you a reason to recognize small quantities and prices. Prices in this adventure are fictional practice examples, not current shop prices.","objectives":["Recognize one, two and three","Ask a price","Read a simple time expression"],"grammar":"いくらですか asks how much something costs. 円 is the currency counter; pronounce 百円 as hyaku-en. Time uses 時: 三時です means it is three o'clock. Counters change how numbers are used, so learn the whole expression.","writing":"Optional: recognize 一, 二 and 三. Say their readings in the phrases instead of assuming every Kanji has only one reading.","roles":[["Numbers 1–10","Numbers 1-10","Your first numbers"],["Numbers 11–100","Numbers 11-100"],["Asking the Time"],["Dates"],["Unit Review"]],"words":[["一","One","ichi"],["二","Two","ni"],["三","Three","san"],["いくらですか。","How much is it?","Ikura desu ka."],["百円です。","It is one hundred yen.","Hyaku-en desu."],["三時です。","It is three o'clock.","San-ji desu."]],"scenario":{"prompt":"You can see the item you want, but cannot find its price. What do you ask?","answer":"いくらですか。","choices":["いくらですか。","三時です。","二"],"explanation":"いくらですか asks a price. 三時です states a time, and 二 is the number two."}},{"slug":"tokyo-guide","location":"Meet Your Tokyo Guide","aliases":["Daily Life"],"culture":"Your guide's name is Aki in this fictional conversation. A short self-introduction often uses a name and です. Personal names are not a reason to ask for legal identity details.","objectives":["Say a chosen name","Ask someone's name politely","Express a simple preference"],"grammar":"A は B です introduces a topic and a polite statement; は is read wa here. In ねこが好きです, が marks what is liked. Subjects can be left unstated when the context is clear. です is not a universal translation of every English 'is'.","writing":"Optional: explore Kana names and the particles は and が in short sentences.","roles":[["Morning Routine"],["Family"],["School & Work"],["Everyday Actions"],["Unit Review"]],"words":[["はじめまして。","Nice to meet you (first meeting).","Hajimemashite."],["アキです。","I am Aki.","Aki desu."],["お名前は何ですか。","What is your name?","Onamae wa nan desu ka."],["よろしくお願いします。","I look forward to getting to know you.","Yoroshiku onegaishimasu."],["ねこが好きです。","I like cats.","Neko ga suki desu."],["私もです。","Me too.","Watashi mo desu."]],"scenario":{"prompt":"Aki introduces themself. You want to ask your next guide's name politely. Choose your question.","answer":"お名前は何ですか。","choices":["お名前は何ですか。","ねこが好きです。","私もです。"],"explanation":"お名前は何ですか asks someone's name; the other choices express a preference or agreement."}},{"slug":"kyoto-tea-house","location":"Kyoto Tea House","aliases":["Food & Eating Out"],"culture":"Tea houses and cafés differ in how they serve guests. This fictional café lets you practice a short order. Ask about ingredients when necessary rather than assuming every dish is suitable for you.","objectives":["Ask for water or tea","Use a polite request","Thank someone after receiving an order"],"grammar":"Noun + をください requests an item. The particle を is pronounced o. 一つ (hitotsu) counts one item in this example: お茶を一つください. Keep the polite request rather than translating English word order literally.","writing":"Optional: compare おちゃ in Hiragana with お茶. Learn 茶 in a word rather than in isolation.","roles":[["Food & Drinks"],["At a Café","At a Cafe"],["Ordering Food"],["Restaurant Conversation"],["Unit Review"]],"words":[["お茶","Tea","ocha"],["水","Water","mizu"],["お茶をください。","Tea, please.","Ocha o kudasai."],["水をください。","Water, please.","Mizu o kudasai."],["お茶を一つください。","One tea, please.","Ocha o hitotsu kudasai."],["ありがとうございます。","Thank you.","Arigatō gozaimasu."]],"scenario":{"prompt":"You are ready to order one tea. Which complete request fits?","answer":"お茶を一つください。","choices":["お茶を一つください。","水をください。","ありがとうございます。"],"explanation":"お茶を一つください requests one tea. 水をください requests water; thanks alone does not place an order."}},{"slug":"tokyo-station","location":"Tokyo Train Station","aliases":["Around the City"],"culture":"Large stations can have many exits. Ask a staff member when unsure, and read the destination as well as the platform. These directional phrases are practice, not real navigation instructions.","objectives":["Ask where a station is","Recognize left and right","Ask someone to repeat slowly"],"grammar":"Place + はどこですか asks where something is. 右 (migi) is right and 左 (hidari) is left. もう一度お願いします is a useful repair phrase when you do not understand the first answer.","writing":"Optional: recognize 駅 on signs and compare 右 and 左.","roles":[["Places in Town","Places to go"],["Asking Where Something Is"],["Directions"],["Finding a Destination"],["Unit Review"]],"words":[["駅","Station","eki"],["駅はどこですか。","Where is the station?","Eki wa doko desu ka."],["右です。","It is on the right.","Migi desu."],["左です。","It is on the left.","Hidari desu."],["まっすぐです。","It is straight ahead.","Massugu desu."],["もう一度お願いします。","Once more, please.","Mō ichido onegaishimasu."]],"scenario":{"prompt":"You missed the staff member's answer. What can you say to ask for it again?","answer":"もう一度お願いします。","choices":["もう一度お願いします。","右です。","駅"],"explanation":"もう一度お願いします asks for repetition; 右です gives a direction rather than asking for clarification."}},{"slug":"osaka-shopping","location":"Osaka Shopping Street","aliases":["Shopping"],"culture":"A shopping street gives you a reason to point out an item and ask its price or color. This is a fictional purchase, and no real currency is involved.","objectives":["Identify an item near you","Ask a price","Ask for an item in a different color"],"grammar":"これ means this thing near the speaker. この must be followed by a noun. In 赤いのはありますか, の stands in for the item being discussed. ありますか asks whether it is available.","writing":"Optional: practice the Kana for colors and notice the adjective ending い in 赤い.","roles":[["Shopping Vocabulary"],["Asking the Price"],["Colors & Sizes","Naming colors"],["Buying Something"],["Unit Review"]],"words":[["これ","This (thing)","kore"],["これはいくらですか。","How much is this?","Kore wa ikura desu ka."],["赤い","Red","akai"],["青い","Blue","aoi"],["赤いのはありますか。","Do you have a red one?","Akai no wa arimasu ka."],["これをください。","This one, please.","Kore o kudasai."]],"scenario":{"prompt":"You like the item but want a red version. Which question should you ask?","answer":"赤いのはありますか。","choices":["赤いのはありますか。","これをください。","青い"],"explanation":"赤いのはありますか asks whether a red one is available. これをください asks to buy the one already indicated."}},{"slug":"kyoto-cultural-walk","location":"Kyoto Cultural Walk","aliases":["Travel & Experiences"],"culture":"Kyoto includes neighborhoods, places of worship, shops and residential streets. Follow the rules displayed at each place; asking permission is better than assuming photography is allowed.","objectives":["Describe a place simply","Ask permission to take a photograph","Ask for help politely"],"grammar":"きれい is a な-adjective: きれいです says something is beautiful or clean. 写真を撮ってもいいですか uses a verb's て-form plus もいいですか to ask permission. Learn it as a useful phrase before studying every verb form.","writing":"Optional: recognize 写真 in context and practice a short sentence with です.","roles":[["At the Station"],["At the Hotel"],["Sightseeing"],["Travel Conversation"],["Unit Review"]],"words":[["きれいです。","It is beautiful / clean.","Kirei desu."],["静かです。","It is quiet.","Shizuka desu."],["写真","Photograph","shashin"],["写真を撮ってもいいですか。","May I take a photograph?","Shashin o totte mo ii desu ka."],["はい、いいですよ。","Yes, that is fine.","Hai, ii desu yo."],["すみません、手伝ってください。","Excuse me, please help me.","Sumimasen, tetsudatte kudasai."]],"scenario":{"prompt":"You would like a picture of an indoor exhibit, but do not know the rules. What should you ask?","answer":"写真を撮ってもいいですか。","choices":["写真を撮ってもいいですか。","静かです。","はい、いいですよ。"],"explanation":"Ask permission with 写真を撮ってもいいですか. Describing a place as quiet is not permission to take a picture."}},{"slug":"japan-explorer-finale","location":"Japan Explorer Finale","aliases":["Beginner Final Journey"],"culture":"Your final fictional day combines greetings, a purchase, a question about location and a request for clarification. Successful communication includes asking for help when needed.","objectives":["Select a phrase for a real-life situation","Combine polite requests with thanks","Repair a conversation when you do not understand"],"grammar":"Use ですか for a polite question, をください for a request, and もう一度お願いします to ask for repetition. These patterns serve different purposes even when they share familiar words.","writing":"Optional: write a three-line travel memory using greetings, a place and a simple preference.","roles":[["Greeting Challenge"],["Daily Life Challenge"],["Food Challenge"],["Travel Challenge"],["Final Beginner Review"]],"words":[["すみません。","Excuse me.","Sumimasen."],["駅はどこですか。","Where is the station?","Eki wa doko desu ka."],["これをください。","This one, please.","Kore o kudasai."],["いくらですか。","How much is it?","Ikura desu ka."],["もう一度お願いします。","Once more, please.","Mō ichido onegaishimasu."],["ありがとうございました。","Thank you (for what you did).","Arigatō gozaimashita."]],"scenario":{"prompt":"You found your item and checked its price. Now you want to buy the item you are pointing at. What do you say?","answer":"これをください。","choices":["これをください。","駅はどこですか。","もう一度お願いします。"],"explanation":"これをください makes the purchase request. The other options ask for a location or for repetition."}}]}$plan$::jsonb;
 unit_plan jsonb; lesson_plan jsonb; lookup_title text; role_plan jsonb; phrase jsonb; target_unit uuid; target_lesson uuid; challenge uuid;
 course uuid := 'c293f603-993b-4332-8dd8-afc0fd50ae04'; country uuid; language uuid; role_index integer; ordering integer;
 lesson_label text; role_names text[]:=array['Discover','Learn','Practice','Real-Life Conversation','Destination Challenge'];
 words_for_lesson jsonb; quiz uuid; existing_word record; lesson_row record; prompt text; options jsonb; key text;
begin
 perform pg_advisory_xact_lock(hashtextextended('acelingua:japan:adventure',0));
 lock table public.units,public.lessons in share row exclusive mode;
 select c.language_id into language from public.courses c join public.languages l on l.id=c.language_id where c.id=course and l.code='ja';
 if language is null then raise exception 'Japan course differs from audit; stop and inspect'; end if;
 select id into strict country from public.travel_countries where code='jp' and is_active;
 if not exists(select 1 from public.travel_country_languages where country_id=country and language_id=language) then raise exception 'Japan/Japanese association missing'; end if;
 for unit_plan in select value from jsonb_array_elements(plan->'units') loop
  if (select count(*) from public.units u where u.course_id=course and (u.title in(select jsonb_array_elements_text(unit_plan->'aliases')) or u.id=md5('ace:adventure:ja:unit:'||(unit_plan->>'slug'))::uuid))>1 then raise exception 'Ambiguous existing unit %',unit_plan->>'slug'; end if;
  select id into target_unit from public.units u where u.course_id=course and (u.title in(select jsonb_array_elements_text(unit_plan->'aliases')) or u.id=md5('ace:adventure:ja:unit:'||(unit_plan->>'slug'))::uuid);
  if target_unit is null then
   select coalesce(max(unit_order),0)+1 into ordering from public.units where course_id=course;
   target_unit:=md5('ace:adventure:ja:unit:'||(unit_plan->>'slug'))::uuid;
   insert into public.units(id,course_id,title,description,unit_order,location_name,is_published)
    values(target_unit,course,unit_plan->>'location',unit_plan->>'culture',ordering,unit_plan->>'location',false);
  end if;
  -- A country display label is additive; existing titles/orders/progress stay intact.
  update public.units set location_name=unit_plan->>'location' where id=target_unit and location_name is null;
  insert into public.travel_country_units(country_id,unit_id,is_required) values(country,target_unit,true) on conflict do nothing;
  role_index:=0; challenge:=null;
  for role_plan in select value from jsonb_array_elements(unit_plan->'roles') loop
   role_index:=role_index+1;
   key:='ace:adventure:ja:'||(unit_plan->>'slug')||':'||role_index::text;
   -- Prefer the stable seed-owned lesson on retries. Legacy drafts remain
   -- unchanged and are never selected as playable adventure roles.
   select id into target_lesson from public.lessons l where l.unit_id=target_unit and l.id=md5(key)::uuid;
   if target_lesson is null then
    if (select count(*) from public.lessons l where l.unit_id=target_unit and l.is_published
     and l.title in(select jsonb_array_elements_text(role_plan)))>1 then raise exception 'Ambiguous published lesson %/%',unit_plan->>'slug',role_index; end if;
    select id into target_lesson from public.lessons l where l.unit_id=target_unit and l.is_published
     and l.title in(select jsonb_array_elements_text(role_plan)) order by l.lesson_order,l.id limit 1;
   end if;
   if target_lesson is null then
    select coalesce(max(lesson_order),0)+1 into ordering from public.lessons where unit_id=target_unit;
    target_lesson:=md5(key)::uuid;
    lesson_label:=role_names[role_index]||' — '||(unit_plan->>'location');
    insert into public.lessons(id,unit_id,title,description,lesson_order,xp_reward,coin_reward,is_published)
    values(target_lesson,target_unit,lesson_label,
      case role_index when 1 then 'Explore the scene and its key expressions. '||(unit_plan->>'culture')
      when 2 then 'Build a useful sentence. '||(unit_plan->>'grammar')
      when 3 then 'Read, recall, and say the expressions without looking. Pronunciation playback uses available browser voices.'
      when 4 then 'Choose a response for a short exchange in this destination. Say both parts aloud.'
      else 'Use this destination’s phrases in a practical assessment. Aim for at least 80 percent correct.' end,
      ordering,20,5,false);
   end if;
   if role_index=5 then challenge:=target_lesson; end if;
   select title into lookup_title from public.lessons where id=target_lesson;
   lesson_plan:=unit_plan||coalesce(plan->'lesson_overrides'->lookup_title,'{}'::jsonb);
   declare unit_plan jsonb:=lesson_plan;
 phrase jsonb; ordering integer; quiz uuid; existing_word record; options jsonb;
begin
   -- Reuse original vocabulary and teaching activities. No UPDATE of learning content.
   if not exists(select 1 from public.vocabulary where lesson_id=target_lesson) then
    for phrase in select value from jsonb_array_elements(unit_plan->'words') with ordinality v(value,n)
     where case when role_index=1 then n<=3 when role_index=2 then n>=3 when role_index=3 then n%2=0 else true end loop
     insert into public.vocabulary(id,lesson_id,word,translation,pronunciation)
      values(md5(target_lesson::text||':word:'||(phrase->>0))::uuid,target_lesson,phrase->>0,phrase->>1,phrase->>2)
      on conflict(id) do nothing;
    end loop;
   end if;
   if not exists(select 1 from public.activities where lesson_id=target_lesson) then
    insert into public.activities(id,lesson_id,title,instructions,activity_type,activity_order)
    values(md5(target_lesson::text||':context')::uuid,target_lesson,'Your destination conversation',
      (unit_plan->>'culture')||E'\n\n'||(unit_plan->>'grammar')||E'\n\n'||
      case role_index when 1 then 'Read the expressions and their translations. Identify who is speaking and why.'
       when 2 then 'Compare the complete phrases. Notice the polite ending and the particles before making your own example.'
       when 3 then 'Read an expression, cover its translation, and recall its meaning. Repeat aloud using pronunciation playback if a voice is available.'
       when 4 then 'Take turns as the traveler and the guide or staff member. Read a request and give an appropriate reply from the expressions.'
       else 'Read each situation carefully. Choose the response that communicates your purpose, not just a familiar-looking word.' end,
      'grammar',1);
   end if;
   if not exists(select 1 from public.questions q join public.activities a on a.id=q.activity_id where a.lesson_id=target_lesson) then
    select coalesce(max(activity_order),0)+1 into ordering from public.activities where lesson_id=target_lesson;
    quiz:=md5(target_lesson::text||':assessment')::uuid;
    insert into public.activities(id,lesson_id,title,instructions,activity_type,activity_order)
     values(quiz,target_lesson,case when role_index=5 then 'Destination Challenge' else 'Put it into practice' end,
     'Read each prompt and choose the meaning or response that fits. Feedback explains each answer. No recorded audio is assumed.','quiz',ordering) on conflict(id) do nothing;
    ordering:=0;
    for existing_word in select * from public.vocabulary where lesson_id=target_lesson order by id limit 4 loop
     ordering:=ordering+1;
     select jsonb_agg(answer order by sort_key,answer) into options from (
      select existing_word.translation as answer,(ordering%3) as sort_key union all
      select translation,case when row_number() over(order by translation)=1 then ((ordering+1)%3) else ((ordering+2)%3) end
      from (select distinct translation from public.vocabulary where lesson_id=target_lesson and translation<>existing_word.translation order by translation limit 2) alternatives
     ) candidates;
     if jsonb_array_length(options)<2 then options:=jsonb_build_array(existing_word.translation,'The speaker is asking something different.'); end if;
     insert into public.questions(id,activity_id,question_text,question_type,correct_answer,options,explanation,question_order)
     values(md5(target_lesson::text||':meaning:'||existing_word.id::text)::uuid,quiz,
      case role_index when 3 then 'Recall the meaning of: ' when 4 then 'In this exchange, what does the speaker communicate with: ' else 'Read the expression. What does it mean: ' end||existing_word.word,
      'multiple_choice',existing_word.translation,options,
      existing_word.word||' means '||existing_word.translation||'. Reading guide: '||coalesce(existing_word.pronunciation,'use the written expression')||'.',ordering) on conflict(id) do nothing;
    end loop;
    if role_index in (4,5) then
     insert into public.questions(id,activity_id,question_text,question_type,correct_answer,options,explanation,question_order)
     values(md5(target_lesson::text||':scenario')::uuid,quiz,unit_plan->'scenario'->>'prompt','multiple_choice',
      unit_plan->'scenario'->>'answer',unit_plan->'scenario'->'choices',unit_plan->'scenario'->>'explanation',ordering+1) on conflict(id) do nothing;
    end if;
   end if;

end;
   -- Only seed-owned new lessons are published. Existing publication flags never change.
   update public.lessons set is_published=true where id=md5(key)::uuid and
    exists(select 1 from public.vocabulary where lesson_id=target_lesson) and
    exists(select 1 from public.questions q join public.activities a on a.id=q.activity_id where a.lesson_id=target_lesson);
  end loop;
  if challenge is null or not exists(select 1 from public.lessons where id=challenge and unit_id=target_unit) then raise exception 'Challenge association invalid'; end if;
  if not exists(select 1 from public.lessons where id=challenge and is_published) then raise exception 'Existing challenge is unpublished; review its publishing decision before seeding this destination'; end if;
  -- Reconcile known supplemental legacy lessons without changing their IDs.
  for lesson_row in select l.id,l.title from public.lessons l where l.unit_id=target_unit and l.is_published
   and (not exists(select 1 from public.vocabulary v where v.lesson_id=l.id)
    or (exists(select 1 from public.activities a where a.lesson_id=l.id) and not exists(select 1 from public.questions q join public.activities a on a.id=q.activity_id where a.lesson_id=l.id))) loop
   if plan->'lesson_overrides' ? lesson_row.title then
    lesson_plan:=unit_plan||(plan->'lesson_overrides'->lesson_row.title);
    target_lesson:=lesson_row.id;
    role_index:=3;
    declare unit_plan jsonb:=lesson_plan;
 phrase jsonb; ordering integer; quiz uuid; existing_word record; options jsonb;
